3 TOP 5 DEEP DIVES

A. agent-discover
The important mechanism is not another MCP registry; it mutates the
active tool universe during the same running agent session. Security
implication: startup-time admission becomes insufficient. Privately
needs capability-delta admission whenever the live tool graph changes.
6m inference: dynamic loading spreads through coding agents. 18m:
agents install capabilities mid-task routinely. 36m: capability
catalogs become effectively unbounded. Smallest test: start with one
tool, dynamically activate a second tool carrying a new external
effect, verify QP notices the reachable-authority delta before first
use. Falsifier: host-level tool catalogs remain immutable or every
dynamic activation reliably triggers native policy admission.

B. Continual Harness
Reset-free modification of prompt/subagents/skills/memory turns
self-improvement into an online control-plane event, not an offline
training event. Security implication: the agent's effective policy can
drift while the task is still executing. Privately should fingerprint
not only tools but the current harness state. Experiment: allow
harmless prompt/skill mutation mid-episode and test whether authority
grants remain semantically valid after harness drift. Falsifier:
adaptations never change reachable effects or decision policy enough
to invalidate prior grants.

C. claw-wrap
This is the cleanest new credential-boundary mechanism this run. The
agent receives CLI semantics but not the credential. The trusted host
executes the sensitive command and can constrain command families.
This suggests Privately should expose narrow capability handles
instead of secrets wherever possible. Experiment: compare env-secret,
network injection and host-command proxy against a benign
prompt-injection exfiltration suite. Metric: secret exposure rate +
legitimate-task completion.

D. Serena CVE-2026-49471
This chain is strategically important because it connects an ordinary
browser trust-boundary failure to persistent agent memory and then
autonomous shell authority. The lesson is not merely 'secure
localhost': persistent memory is an executable future-input channel.
Privately should model memory writes as delayed capability-bearing
events. Safe experiment: toy local dashboard, synthetic memory store
and harmless marker action only; test whether origin/auth +
memory-admission layers independently stop the chain.

E. multimodal-mcp
This is close to the media architecture Privately needs: a single
agent-facing media surface can choose across Sora/Grok/Veo plus
image/audio providers. It lacks the full research=E2=86=92publish loop, but=
 is
a strong substrate. Experiment: one fixed 30-second Privately script,
route equivalent shot prompts across three providers, score
cost/latency/visual adherence, then feed winner into deterministic
edit/caption stage.

